                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "xouGp",
                          "x": 0,
                          "y": 0,
                          "name": "Rebranding at Scale",
                          "metadata": {
                            "type": "figma-import",
                            "nodeId": "1:278",
                            "sourcePath": "1:888/1:216/1:217/1:276/1:277/1:278"
                          },
                          "fill": "$text-primary",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                          "width": 640,
                          "height": 40,
                          "content": "Rebranding at Scale",
                          "lineHeight": 1,
                          "fontFamily": "Averia Serif Libre",
                          "fontSize": 40,
                          "fontWeight": "700",
                          "letterSpacing": -2.4000000953674316,
                          "fontStyle": "italic"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "X84O8h",
                          "x": 0,
                          "y": 72,
                          "name": "When the client decided to reposition the product, I took responsibility for updating its visual identity across a large, established application. Before starting the rebrand, I proposed four approaches ranging from a lightweight visual refresh to a more comprehensive UI redesign. Each option included visual examples, explanations of the proposed changes, and their scope and trade-offs. The client chose a lighter approach focused primarily on refreshing the visual language rather than rebuilding the entire interface.",
                          "metadata": {
                            "type": "figma-import",
                            "nodeId": "1:279",
                            "sourcePath": "1:888/1:216/1:217/1:276/1:277/1:279"
                          },
                          "fill": "$text-primary",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                          "width": 640,
                          "height": 308,
                          "content": "When the client decided to reposition the product, I took responsibility \nfor updating its visual identity across a large, established application.\n\nBefore starting the rebrand, I proposed four approaches ranging from a \nlightweight visual refresh to a more comprehensive UI redesign.\n\nEach option included visual examples, explanations of the proposed \nchanges, and their scope and trade-offs.\n\nThe client chose a lighter approach focused primarily on refreshing the \nvisual language rather than rebuilding the entire interface.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.399999976158142,
                          "fontFamily": "Averia Serif Libre",
                          "fontSize": 20,
                          "fontWeight": "300",
                          "letterSpacing": -0.4000000059604645
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "okyjW",
                      "x": 0,
                      "y": 460,
                      "name": "Frame 10",
                      "metadata": {
                        "type": "figma-import",
                        "nodeId": "1:280",
                        "sourcePath": "1:888/1:216/1:217/1:276/1:280"
                      },
                      "width": 1024,
                      "height": 1032,
                      "layout": "none",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "frame",
                          "id": "raveW",
                          "x": 192,
                          "y": 0,
                          "name": "bio",
                          "metadata": {
                            "type": "figma-import",
                            "nodeId": "1:281",
                            "sourcePath": "1:888/1:216/1:217/1:276/1:280/1:281"
                          },
                          "width": 640,
                          "height": 344,
                          "layout": "none",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "MeZFv",
                              "x": 0,
                              "y": 0,
                              "name": "Applying the new visual direction",
                              "metadata": {
                                "type": "figma-import",
                                "nodeId": "1:282",
                                "sourcePath": "1:888/1:216/1:217/1:276/1:280/1:281/1:282"
                              },
                              "fill": "$text-primary",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                              "width": 640,
                              "height": 32,
                              "content": "Applying the new visual direction",
                              "lineHeight": 1,
                              "fontFamily": "Averia Serif Libre",
                              "fontSize": 32,
                              "fontWeight": "700",
                              "letterSpacing": -2,
                              "fontStyle": "italic"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "tuXah",
                              "x": 0,
                              "y": 64,
                              "name": "The biggest challenge was applying the updated visual direction consistently across hundreds of existing designs while product development continued. I used the component library to update shared styles, colors, and UI elements across the application, then reviewed and refined individual screens according to their priority and requirements. This helped make a large-scale update more manageable without redesigning every screen from scratch.",
                              "metadata": {
                                "type": "figma-import",
                                "nodeId": "1:283",
                                "sourcePath": "1:888/1:216/1:217/1:276/1:280/1:281/1:283"
                              },
                              "fill": "$text-primary",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                              "width": 640,
                              "height": 280,
                              "content": "The biggest challenge was applying the updated visual direction \nconsistently across hundreds of existing designs while product \ndevelopment continued.\n\nI used the component library to update shared styles, colors, and UI \nelements across the application, then reviewed and refined individual \nscreens according to their priority and requirements.\n\nThis helped make a large-scale update more manageable without \nredesigning every screen from scratch.",
                              "lineHeight": 1.399999976158142,
                              "fontFamily": "Averia Serif Libre",
                              "fontSize": 20,
                              "fontWeight": "300",
                              "letterSpacing": -0.4000000059604645
                            }
                          ]
                        },
