                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "Y4BwY",
                      "x": 192,
                      "y": 0,
                      "name": "bio",
                      "metadata": {
                        "type": "figma-import",
                        "nodeId": "1:640",
                        "sourcePath": "1:889/1:578/1:579/1:639/1:640"
                      },
                      "width": 640,
                      "height": 464,
                      "layout": "none",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "rbVPd",
                          "x": 0,
                          "y": 0,
                          "name": "Less navigation, more playing",
                          "metadata": {
                            "type": "figma-import",
                            "nodeId": "1:641",
                            "sourcePath": "1:889/1:578/1:579/1:639/1:640/1:641"
                          },
                          "fill": "$text-primary",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                          "width": 640,
                          "height": 40,
                          "content": "Less navigation, more playing",
                          "lineHeight": 1,
                          "fontFamily": "Averia Serif Libre",
                          "fontSize": 40,
                          "fontWeight": "700",
                          "letterSpacing": -2.4000000953674316,
                          "fontStyle": "italic"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "AE0bU",
                          "x": 0,
                          "y": 72,
                          "name": "Another important decision was simplifying how children move between activities. Instead of relying on traditional navigation, I designed the game menu as a central hub connecting the entire experience. Each game consists of five short rounds. After completing them, children automatically return to the hub, where a friendly voice invites them to choose another activity. They can also leave a game early or replay it. This repeatable loop reduces unnecessary navigation decisions and makes moving between games feel natural.",
                          "metadata": {
                            "type": "figma-import",
                            "nodeId": "1:642",
                            "sourcePath": "1:889/1:578/1:579/1:639/1:640/1:642"
                          },
                          "fill": "$text-primary",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                          "width": 640,
                          "height": 392,
                          "content": "Another important decision was simplifying how children move between \nactivities.\n\nInstead of relying on traditional navigation, I designed the game menu as \na central hub connecting the entire experience.\n\nEach game consists of five short rounds. After completing them, children \nautomatically return to the hub, where a friendly voice invites them to \nchoose another activity.\n\nThey can also leave a game early or replay it.\n\nThis repeatable loop reduces unnecessary navigation decisions and makes \nmoving between games feel natural.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.399999976158142,
                          "fontFamily": "Averia Serif Libre",
                          "fontSize": 20,
                          "fontWeight": "300",
                          "letterSpacing": -0.4000000059604645
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "q2qBGk",
                      "type": "ref",
                      "ref": "s37h6",
                      "name": "frame-image",
                      "x": 0,
                      "y": 512,
                      "width": 1024,
                      "height": 640,
                      "fill": [
                        "$background-secondary",
                        {
                          "type": "image",
                          "enabled": true,
                          "url": "original-assets/a2e50091488e15f8fa7e61ec6cf86eb4b397b694.png",
                          "mode": "cover"
                        }
                      ],
                      "cornerRadius": 16,
                      "layout": "none",
                      "clip": true
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "z5EHY",
                  "x": 0,
                  "y": 5936,
                  "name": "Frame 19",
                  "metadata": {
                    "type": "figma-import",
                    "nodeId": "1:644",
                    "sourcePath": "1:889/1:578/1:579/1:644"
                  },
                  "width": 1024,
                  "height": 1152,
                  "layout": "none",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "wdWW7",
                      "x": 192,
                      "y": 0,
                      "name": "bio",
                      "metadata": {
                        "type": "figma-import",
                        "nodeId": "1:645",
                        "sourcePath": "1:889/1:578/1:579/1:644/1:645"
                      },
                      "width": 640,
                      "height": 464,
                      "layout": "none",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "jIPKw",
                          "x": 0,
                          "y": 0,
                          "name": "A playful world built from scratch",
                          "metadata": {
                            "type": "figma-import",
                            "nodeId": "1:646",
                            "sourcePath": "1:889/1:578/1:579/1:644/1:645/1:646"
                          },
                          "fill": "$text-primary",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                          "width": 640,
                          "height": 40,
                          "content": "A playful world built from scratch",
                          "lineHeight": 1,
                          "fontFamily": "Averia Serif Libre",
                          "fontSize": 40,
                          "fontWeight": "700",
                          "letterSpacing": -2.4000000953674316,
                          "fontStyle": "italic"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "Q0mlPN",
                          "x": 0,
                          "y": 72,
                          "name": "With no existing brand or visual system, I created Zuzuzoo's visual identity from the ground up. The direction focused on warmth, simplicity, and playful character – combining friendly animal illustrations, bright colors, soft shapes, and large interactive elements. Illustrations became an essential part of the visual language, helping children recognize activities and making the experience feel more engaging and approachable. I also developed a lightweight design system to maintain consistency across iPhone, iPad, the new foldable iPhone Duo, and Android devices, keeping components and interaction patterns intentionally simple.",
                          "metadata": {
                            "type": "figma-import",
                            "nodeId": "1:647",
                            "sourcePath": "1:889/1:578/1:579/1:644/1:645/1:647"
                          },
                          "fill": "$text-primary",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                          "width": 640,
                          "height": 392,
                          "content": "With no existing brand or visual system, I created Zuzuzoo's visual \nidentity from the ground up.\n\nThe direction focused on warmth, simplicity, and playful character – \ncombining friendly animal illustrations, bright colors, soft shapes, and \nlarge interactive elements.\n\nIllustrations became an essential part of the visual language, helping \nchildren recognize activities and making the experience feel more \nengaging and approachable.\n\nI also developed a lightweight design system to maintain consistency \nacross iPhone, iPad, the new foldable iPhone Duo, and Android devices, \nkeeping components and interaction patterns intentionally simple.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.399999976158142,
                          "fontFamily": "Averia Serif Libre",
                          "fontSize": 20,
                          "fontWeight": "300",
                          "letterSpacing": -0.4000000059604645
                        }
                      ]
                    },
